  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Arizona has received $24.7B in federal contract obligations so far in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 14,955 awards with an average award size of $1.7M, and obligations rose up 5.9% year over year. The Department of Defense leads buying activity with $17.4B in obligations, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $6B. Top vendors include RAYTHEON COMPANY with $8B, TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP with $4.7B, and FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO with $4.5B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $6.3B, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $6B and Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers at $4.7B. Historical obligations show variability: FY21 recorded $16.5B, FY22 recorded $15.3B, FY23 recorded $19.8B, FY24 recorded $18B, and FY25 recorded $23.3B. This fiscal year to date total of $24.7B reflects the current partial-year activity and the concentration of spending in defense, construction, and health-related contracts.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting in Arizona changed year over year?",
        "body": "Arizona obligations rose up 5.9% year over year in FY2026 to date. Obligations reached $24.7B in FY26, building on prior-year totals of $23.3B in FY25 and earlier totals of $18B in FY24 and $19.8B in FY23. The state recorded 14,955 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $1.7M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries drive Arizona federal contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $17.4B in Arizona during FY2026 to date, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $6B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing led industries with $6.3B, Commercial and Institutional Building Construction followed with $6B, and Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers recorded $4.7B. Major vendors supporting that activity include RAYTHEON COMPANY with $8B and TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP with $4.7B."
      }
    ]
  },
